Subject: launcher: centre presentation terminals without relying on --app-id

Omarchy floats, centres and sizes its presentation terminals -- the windows
behind every privileged menu row -- with class rules:

    o.window("(org.omarchy.terminal|...)", { tag = "+floating-window" })

and `omarchy-launch-floating-terminal-with-presentation` earns that class by
passing `--app-id=org.omarchy.terminal` to xdg-terminal-exec.

That cannot work with QTerminal, the terminal this install uses. QTerminal
2.4.0's entire command line is `-d -e -h -p -v -w`: no class, no app-id, no
title. Qt hardcodes the application name, so even exec'ing it through a
symlink named `org.omarchy.terminal` still maps as class "qterminal"
(measured). The class rules never match, and privileged prompts tile like any
other window instead of appearing centred over the desktop.

Rather than change the terminal, attach the rules to the window at spawn time:

    hyprctl dispatch 'hl.dsp.exec_cmd("[float;center;size 875 600] ...")'

which is terminal-agnostic. Verified that the association survives the
uwsm-app handoff -- Hyprland walks the spawned process tree, so entering a
systemd scope does not break it -- and that the result is geometrically
identical to the class-rule path: float=true, 875x600 at [523,253] on a
1920x1080 output, from both routes.

The presentation script travels via a temp file in XDG_RUNTIME_DIR rather than
being embedded in the dispatch string: it contains quotes, semicolons and `$?`
and would otherwise have to survive both Lua string quoting and Hyprland's
`sh -c`. The temp file removes itself through an EXIT trap. The child
re-establishes PATH and gum styling itself, because Hyprland spawns it and it
inherits Hyprland's environment rather than the launcher's.

If the dispatch is ever refused -- a Lua API change after a Hyprland upgrade --
the script falls through to the upstream exec, so the prompt still appears,
just not centred.

Drop this patch if the default terminal ever moves to one that can set its own
app_id (kitty is installed and takes --class); the class rules in
config/hypr/omarchy4.lua already cover that case and need no change.
---
--- a/bin/omarchy-launch-floating-terminal-with-presentation
+++ b/bin/omarchy-launch-floating-terminal-with-presentation
@@ -10,4 +10,44 @@ source omarchy-restart-gum
 cmd="$*"
 presentation_script="omarchy-show-logo; $cmd; if (( \$? != 130 )); then omarchy-show-done; fi"
 
+# Upstream depends on --app-id=org.omarchy.terminal so that the class rules in
+# hypr/apps/system.lua float, centre and size this window. QTerminal 2.4.0 --
+# the terminal this install uses -- offers no way to set a Wayland app_id (its
+# only flags are -d -e -h -p -v -w, and Qt hardcodes the application name, so
+# even invoking it through a renamed symlink still maps as class "qterminal").
+# The class rules therefore never match and privileged prompts tile like any
+# other window.
+#
+# Attach the rules to the window this exec spawns instead. That is
+# terminal-agnostic, and it survives the uwsm-app handoff: Hyprland walks the
+# spawned process tree, so moving into a systemd scope does not break the
+# association.
+#
+# The presentation script travels via a temp file rather than being embedded in
+# the dispatch string -- it contains quotes, semicolons and `$?`, which would
+# otherwise have to survive both Lua string quoting and Hyprland's `sh -c`.
+# The child re-establishes PATH and gum styling itself, because it is spawned
+# by Hyprland and inherits Hyprland's environment, not this script's.
+if [[ -n ${HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE:-} ]] && command -v hyprctl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+  runner=$(mktemp -p "${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}" omarchy-present.XXXXXXXX)
+  chmod 700 "$runner"
+  {
+    echo '#!/bin/bash'
+    echo 'trap '\''rm -f -- "$0"'\'' EXIT'
+    echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/share/omarchy/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"'
+    echo 'source omarchy-restart-gum'
+    echo "$presentation_script"
+  } >"$runner"
+
+  if [[ $(hyprctl dispatch \
+      "hl.dsp.exec_cmd(\"[float;center;size 875 600] uwsm-app -- xdg-terminal-exec --app-id=org.omarchy.terminal --title=Omarchy -e $runner\")" \
+      2>&1) == ok* ]]; then
+    exit 0
+  fi
+
+  # Dispatch refused (Lua API drift after a Hyprland upgrade?) -- fall through
+  # to the upstream path so the prompt still appears, just not centred.
+  rm -f -- "$runner"
+fi
+
 exec setsid uwsm-app -- xdg-terminal-exec --app-id=org.omarchy.terminal --title=Omarchy -e bash -c "$presentation_script"
